title: Review of the Protection
subtitle: The cabinet's partners want to cut the benefit.
new-page: true
tags: pl_event
face-image: img/polish/polish_event_austerity_1926.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishProjects.austerityEventDue(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Event cabinet.austerity_1926 (technical reference 17.13 B19, 17.16.4; card catalogue 9.13): once, in
// I–IV 1926 — the review in the sixth month of Skrzyński's cabinet with a full protection of 2 B, or a
// budget below −2 B for two months. The four answers of the government-support card (9.8), for 0 T.
Q.pl_aus_threat = 0;
!}

= The review of the protection

The partners on the right propose to limit the protection for the unemployed from 2 B to 1 B a month — a programme demand, also while the budget can pay. The one compromise keeps 2 B with the existing or a lawfully improved financing. A cut needs a change of the law and gives only +1 B.

- @bargain
- @persuade
- @maintain
- @withdraw

@bargain
title: Demand the full protection, or we end our support
subtitle: The partners weigh how much they need PPS; those who give in think less of us (−3 relation).
on-arrival: {!
var out = PolishProjects.austerityChoose(Q, 'bargain');
Q.pl_aus_threat = out.threat ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_aus_result = (out.accepted ? 'The partners accept: the protection stays at 2 B.' : 'The partners refuse.') + ' ' +
    PolishGovernment.describeAnswers({evaluations: out.evaluations});
!}
go-to: threat if pl_aus_threat; result if not pl_aus_threat

@persuade
title: Persuade them without a threat
subtitle: The same offer; no relation change either way. If refused, the cut goes to the vote.
on-arrival: {!
var out = PolishProjects.austerityChoose(Q, 'persuade');
Q.pl_aus_result = out.accepted ? 'The partners accept: the protection stays at 2 B. ' + PolishGovernment.describeAnswers({evaluations: out.evaluations}) :
    'The partners refuse. ' + (out.cut.status === 'rejected' ? 'The cut finds no majority; the protection stays.' : 'The Sejm adopts the cut: the protection falls to 1 B.');
!}
go-to: result

@maintain
title: Keep our support despite the dispute
subtitle: The cut passes if it has support.
on-arrival: {!
var out = PolishProjects.austerityChoose(Q, 'maintain');
Q.pl_aus_result = out.cut.status === 'rejected' ? 'The cut finds no majority; the protection stays at 2 B.' : 'The Sejm adopts the cut: the protection falls to 1 B.';
!}
go-to: result

@withdraw
title: Withdraw our support
subtitle: PPS leaves; the cabinet may stay if the rest of its base accepts the programme.
on-arrival: {!
var out = PolishProjects.austerityChoose(Q, 'withdraw');
Q.pl_aus_result = out.fell ? 'PPS leaves and the cabinet resigns.' : 'PPS leaves the cabinet. It governs without PPS unless the Sejm dismisses it.';
!}
go-to: result

@threat
new-page: true

= The partners refuse

[+ pl_aus_result +]

A threat must be real. We decide now, without spending another month.

- @carry_out
- @back_down

@carry_out
title: Carry out the threat: end our support
on-arrival: {!
var out = PolishProjects.austerityThreat(Q, 'carry_out');
Q.pl_aus_result = out.fell ? 'PPS leaves and the cabinet resigns.' : 'PPS leaves the cabinet.';
!}
go-to: result

@back_down
title: Back down
subtitle: Our reputation falls (−5); the cut goes to the vote; later threats against this cabinet count only as persuasion.
on-arrival: {!
var out = PolishProjects.austerityThreat(Q, 'back_down');
Q.pl_aus_result = out.cut.status === 'rejected' ? 'We back down. The cut finds no majority; the protection stays.' : 'We back down. The Sejm adopts the cut: the protection falls to 1 B.';
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state

= The review of the protection

[+ pl_aus_result +]

- @root: Continue.
